{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30169 - PROTEIN:5944",
  "verbalization": "Leosibirone B, (rel)- is implicated in the regulation of Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Leosibirone B acts as a target of several compounds, which in turn target the kinase activity of Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8. Specifically, Leosibirone B is linked to Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which is a target of WS-5995 B, and both of these are targets of the compound (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan, which also targets Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8. Additionally, Leosibirone B is directly linked to CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a target of 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, another compound that targets the same kinase. These findings suggest that Leosibirone B may modulate the activity of Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 through a series of molecular interactions, potentially influencing downstream signaling pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with Leosibirone B acting as a mediator in the regulation of this kinase. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Leosibirone B and Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
